From: TB710FU clean board
Subject: [PATCH] Keep overlapping PRELINKTEXT mappings unhinted

Source: pinned XNU ac9718fb1af618d5ce8678d0dc6e8a58f252216f after device
patch 0028 in arm_vm_init.c. The device fileset nests native __TEXT within
the outer __PRELINK_TEXT. Initial native __TEXT mapping can set the L3
contiguous hint bit, while PRELINKTEXT RNX finalization builds entries
with that bit clear and asserts equality against existing live PTEs.

Set the initial granule policy before the tables go live. Keep ARM64
block eligibility, RNX flags and the active-map checks. Disjoint native
TEXT mappings continue to allow hints.

Verification: exact source replay, host geometry/policy cases, and the
official macOS native link and strict prelink workflow.
---

diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
index f03c10dfc3e7c860d490747973b009c2e1c37c94..bd948b65ebc6c8b558ac8a924fcc5e0ae6802315 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
@@ -1912,7 +1912,17 @@ noAuxKC:
 	 *
 	 * TEXT segment contains mach headers and other non-executable data. This will become RONX later.
 	 */
-	arm_vm_page_granular_RNX(segTEXTB, segSizeTEXT, ARM64_GRANULE_ALLOW_BLOCK | ARM64_GRANULE_ALLOW_HINT);
+	/* A fileset may place the native __TEXT inside the coalesced kext TEXT.
+	 * That region is tightened again after the tables go live, without hints.
+	 * Keep both passes consistent for the overlapping native TEXT mapping.
+	 */
+	unsigned text_granule = ARM64_GRANULE_ALLOW_BLOCK;
+	if (segSizePRELINKTEXT == 0 || segSizeTEXT == 0 ||
+	    (segTEXTB >= segPRELINKTEXTB && segTEXTB - segPRELINKTEXTB >= segSizePRELINKTEXT) ||
+	    (segTEXTB < segPRELINKTEXTB && segPRELINKTEXTB - segTEXTB >= segSizeTEXT)) {
+		text_granule |= ARM64_GRANULE_ALLOW_HINT;
+	}
+	arm_vm_page_granular_RNX(segTEXTB, segSizeTEXT, text_granule);
 
 	/* Can DATACONST start out and stay RNX?
 	 * NO, stuff in this segment gets modified during startup (viz. mac_policy_init()/mac_policy_list)
